<urn:atm:triage:finding/YB-026>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "YB-026" ;
  triage:title "RSH-Y9-001: blocking FS I/O in non_claude_outbound_runtime.rs without spawn_blocking" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/non_claude_outbound_runtime.rs:49-104 performs blocking FS I/O (fs::create_dir_all, OpenOptions::open, write_all, sync_data) without spawn_blocking wrapper. Trait is synchronous by contract (fn deliver_payloads(&self, ...) -> Result); callers expect synchronous execution semantics. spawn_blocking would violate the trait contract. Team-lead preliminary ruling: waived as not applicable to synchronous trait implementations." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-Yb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "RSH" ;
  triage:severity "Important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "waived" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:waiverReason "synchronous_trait_contract" ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-05-17T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:triagedBy "qa-triage-agent" ;
  triage:notes "NonClaudeOutbound trait is fully synchronous (no async fn, no Future return type). The impl intentionally performs blocking I/O within the synchronous method body per the trait contract. RSH-Y9-001 (spawn_blocking for blocking I/O) only applies to async execution contexts where blocking calls could stall the tokio runtime. In a synchronous trait, blocking I/O is the expected execution model." .

